{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Within the city</b> Rabbi Abraham [Ibn Ezra] explained that they fear HaShem in public, as it says, \"Run to and fro through the streets of Jerusalem\" (Jeremiah 5:1). But the correct interpretation in my eyes is that Abraham said \"within the city,\" meaning that even if there are foreigners within it, it is fitting that they rescue it. And he said this for the sake of Lot, thinking that perhaps there are others there:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:31:44.573386183Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}